# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# When the auction itself forces to game (Rick, 2026-09-30): "we should
# have a state 'in game force' that 2/1 triggers, or 4th suit forcing,
# or XYZ 2D, etc." The state is `we.forcing = game`. A rule whose call
# creates it says so with `sets forcing=game` (the two-over-one on a 2/1
# card, a strong jump shift); the declarations here are the forces that
# belong to the shape of the auction rather than to one rule's meaning,
# and apply whichever rule made or explains the call.

module game-force "When the auction forces to game"
  needs  base
  skill  bidding_conventions/two_over_one
  param  wolff = other_conventions.wolff_signoff.play default false

# Responder's third bid at the three level, below game: "a 3rd bid by
# responder at the 3 level or higher is usually considered a GF" (Rick).
# 3NT and higher are game themselves.
force game when partner.opened, !they.bid, me.bids = 2, call >= 3C, call <= 3S

# After opener's 2NT rebid (18-19), anything but pass forces to game,
# except Wolff's 3C, which is there to stop in a part score.
force game after 1x (P) 1y (P) 2N (P) when !call = P, !(wolff, call = 3C)
